$$ kd-init.kd - symbol setup. Replay after every guest reboot.
$$
$$     python tools/kdc.py --file tools/kd-init.kd --timeout 150
$$
$$ THE SYMBOL PATH DOES NOT SURVIVE A NEW kd SESSION. kdd.py replays
$$ nothing on connect, so a VM reboot that restarts the debugger leaves
$$ the path empty again - and an empty path is not an error, it is a
$$ stack trace full of bare addresses that reads as a corrupt stack.
$$
$$ Two entries, and both are needed:
$$   the Microsoft store  - ntoskrnl, hidclass, usbport. Without these
$$                          every frame through the kernel is an address.
$$   our own build output - xboxctl.sys.pdb, so our frames carry function
$$                          names and source lines. The linker writes it
$$                          beside the .sys; /Z7 puts the rest in the objs.
$$
$$ THE SECOND PATH IS THE HOST'S, NOT THE GUEST'S. kd runs on the host, so
$$ it reads the build tree directly - the .pdb never has to be copied into
$$ the VM, and must not be, since a stale copy there would be found first.

.sympath srv*C:\symbols*https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols;N:\DEV\XBOXCTL\src_drv\build\x64\Release
.reload

$$ Proof the path took. nt must say "pdb symbols", not "export symbols"
$$ and not "no symbols".
lm m nt

$$ Our driver, once it is installed. Before that this prints nothing,
$$ which is the correct answer rather than a failure.
lm vm xboxctl
